  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Oblonganoside C and MAP kinase-activated protein kinase 2 (MAPK2) through multiple indirect pathways. Oblonganoside C is identified as a target of several compounds, including Ent-Gloeosteretriol and Theasaponin E1, which in turn target MAPK2. Additionally, Oblonganoside C is also linked to Caov-4, which is a target of K-252a, another compound that also targets MAPK2. These findings collectively indicate that Oblonganoside C may influence MAPK2 through different downstream targets, potentially modulating its activity in various cellular contexts. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Oblonganoside C affects MAPK2 remains to be elucidated. The evidence highlights the complexity of the signaling pathways involved and underscores the need for further experimental validation to confirm the direct interaction between Oblonganoside C and MAPK2.",
